The SERP for this keyword is dominated by two types of content: (1) directory/listing pages from student housing platforms (UTSA's official off-campus housing marketplace, College Pads, AmberStudent, ForRentUniversity, Uloop) and (2) individual property landing pages from purpose-built student housing communities (Prado, Hill Country Place, Villas at Babcock, Campus Edge, High View, Lark San Antonio, etc.).

There is no informational guide, comparison article, or practical renter resource ranking in the top results. Every competitor is either a listing directory or a property marketing page. This is a direct content gap.

**Format decision:** This article should be a practical renter's guide structured as a localized comparison with named options, real price ranges, and decision frameworks. This format does not currently appear in the top results, creates clear differentiation, and matches the informational layer of the searcher's intent (before they choose a specific property). It also positions brightplace as a knowledgeable neutral party rather than a listing aggregator.

